IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pa-enforcement-appeals`

-- Planning Act 1998, ss 21, 22, 28 to 30, 34 and 42(3) -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_pa.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a served owner who ignored the notice` MEANS NoticeStatus WITH
    `was served the notice` IS TRUE
    `complied` IS FALSE
    `later resumed the prohibited use or reinstated the works` IS FALSE
    `superseded by a permission or withdrawn` IS FALSE

`a served owner who complied` MEANS NoticeStatus WITH
    `was served the notice` IS TRUE
    `complied` IS TRUE
    `later resumed the prohibited use or reinstated the works` IS FALSE
    `superseded by a permission or withdrawn` IS FALSE

`a served owner who complied then resumed short-term lets` MEANS NoticeStatus WITH
    `was served the notice` IS TRUE
    `complied` IS TRUE
    `later resumed the prohibited use or reinstated the works` IS TRUE
    `superseded by a permission or withdrawn` IS FALSE

`a new owner who resumed the use` MEANS NoticeStatus WITH
    `was served the notice` IS FALSE
    `complied` IS FALSE
    `later resumed the prohibited use or reinstated the works` IS TRUE
    `superseded by a permission or withdrawn` IS FALSE

`an owner whose use was later permitted` MEANS NoticeStatus WITH
    `was served the notice` IS TRUE
    `complied` IS FALSE
    `later resumed the prohibited use or reinstated the works` IS FALSE
    `superseded by a permission or withdrawn` IS TRUE

`an appeal on day 10 of a 14-day notice` MEANS NoticeAppeal WITH
    `days since service` IS 10
    `days until the notice takes effect` IS 14

`an appeal on day 15 of a 14-day notice` MEANS NoticeAppeal WITH
    `days since service` IS 15
    `days until the notice takes effect` IS 14

§ `ss 21, 22`

#ASSERT `an appeal to the Minister lies` `a refusal` 30
#ASSERT `an appeal to the Minister lies` `a grant with conditions` 30
#ASSERT `an appeal to the Minister lies` `a conditional provisional permission` 30
#ASSERT `an appeal to the Minister lies` `a cancellation` 30
#ASSERT NOT `an appeal to the Minister lies` `a called-in decision of the Minister` 30
#ASSERT NOT `an appeal to the Minister lies` `a grant without conditions` 30
#ASSERT `an appeal to the Minister lies` `a refusal` 60
#ASSERT NOT `an appeal to the Minister lies` `a refusal` 61

#ASSERT NOT `a court may question the Minister's decision` `a refusal`
#ASSERT NOT `a court may question the Minister's decision` `a grant with conditions`
#ASSERT NOT `a court may question the Minister's decision` `a conditional provisional permission`
#ASSERT NOT `a court may question the Minister's decision` `a cancellation`
#ASSERT NOT `a court may question the Minister's decision` `a called-in decision of the Minister`

#ASSERT NOT `an appeal against a refusal or conditions suspends enforcement` FALSE
#ASSERT `an appeal against a refusal or conditions suspends enforcement` TRUE

§ `ss 28 to 30`

#ASSERT `the enforcement notice appeal is in time` `an appeal on day 10 of a 14-day notice`
#ASSERT NOT `the enforcement notice appeal is in time` `an appeal on day 15 of a 14-day notice`

#ASSERT `the notice gives the minimum period` 14
#ASSERT NOT `the notice gives the minimum period` 13

#ASSERT `the person commits an enforcement notice offence` `a served owner who ignored the notice`
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits an enforcement notice offence` `a served owner who complied`
#ASSERT `the person commits an enforcement notice offence` `a served owner who complied then resumed short-term lets`
#ASSERT `the person commits an enforcement notice offence` `a new owner who resumed the use`
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits an enforcement notice offence` `an owner whose use was later permitted`

#ASSERT NOT `compliance has discharged the notice` `a served owner who complied`

#ASSERT `the notice's validity may be questioned in the forum` `an appeal to the Minister under section 29`
#ASSERT NOT `the notice's validity may be questioned in the forum` `judicial review`
#ASSERT NOT `the notice's validity may be questioned in the forum` `a defence in the prosecution`

§ `s 34 -- civil penalty`

#ASSERT `the maximum civil penalty` 1000 EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `the maximum civil penalty` 3000 EQUALS 150000
#ASSERT `the maximum civil penalty` 5000 EQUALS 150000

#ASSERT NOT `a section 12 prosecution may still proceed` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a section 12 prosecution may still proceed` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `a section 12 prosecution may still proceed` FALSE TRUE

§ `s 42(3)`

#ASSERT `the tenant may deduct it from rent and keep possession` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the tenant may deduct it from rent and keep possession` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the tenant may deduct it from rent and keep possession` FALSE FALSE

